{"id": "swebq0006", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.51, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2418, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "United States District Court for the Eastern District of New York", "query": "where to get a marriage license in long island?", "transcript": "Where to get a marriage license in Long Island?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "To get a marriage license in Long Island, you'll want to visit the Town Clerk or City Clerk’s office for either Nassau or Suffolk County. In New York State, any town or city clerk can issue the license, and it's valid anywhere in the state. For example, you might go to the Town of Hempstead Clerk in Nassau County, or the Town of Babylon Clerk in Suffolk County. Generally, both people getting married need to appear together in person with proper identification and proof of age, pay a fee—usually around $40—and wait 24 hours before the ceremony. I'd recommend checking the specific town or city clerk’s website or giving them a call ahead of time to confirm their exact requirements and procedures.", "expert_answer": "In Long Island, you get a marriage license from a **Town Clerk or City Clerk’s office** in **Nassau or Suffolk County**. In New York State, you can apply at **any town or city clerk’s office**, and the license is valid anywhere in NY.\n\nExamples:\n\n- **Nassau County:** Town of Hempstead Clerk, Town of North Hempstead Clerk, Town of Oyster Bay Clerk, City of Long Beach Clerk, City of Glen Cove Clerk  \n- **Suffolk County:** Town of Babylon Clerk, Brookhaven Clerk, Huntington Clerk, Islip Clerk, Smithtown Clerk, Southampton Clerk, East Hampton Clerk, Riverhead Clerk, Southold Clerk, Shelter Island Clerk\n\nGeneral requirements:\n- Both applicants usually must appear in person\n- Bring government photo ID and proof of age\n- Fee is typically about **$40**\n- There is a **24-hour waiting period**\n- License is valid for **60 days**\n\nYou should check the specific town or city clerk’s website or call ahead, as appointments and document requirements can vary.", "expert_latency_s": 9.11, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 3673}
{"id": "swebq0009", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.09, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1727, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Shannon Pot", "query": "where does the shannon river start and end?", "transcript": "Where does the Shannon River start and end?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The River Shannon starts at the **Shannon Pot**, a small pool on the slopes of **Cuilcagh Mountain in County Cavan, Ireland**. It flows south and southwest through Ireland and ends by emptying into the **Atlantic Ocean via the Shannon Estuary**, between **Loop Head in County Clare** and **Kerry Head in County Kerry**.", "expert_answer": "The River Shannon starts at the **Shannon Pot**, a small pool on the slopes of **Cuilcagh Mountain in County Cavan, Ireland**.\n\nIt flows south and southwest through Ireland and ends by emptying into the **Atlantic Ocean via the Shannon Estuary**, between **Loop Head in County Clare** and **Kerry Head in County Kerry**.", "expert_latency_s": 4.7, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1655}
