{"id": "swebq0078", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.46, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1926, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "School of Mathematics, Institute for Advanced Study;Humboldt University of Berlin Department of Physics", "query": "what colleges did albert einstein teach at?", "transcript": "What colleges did Albert Einstein teach at?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Albert Einstein held teaching positions at several notable institutions throughout his career. He served as a professor or lecturer at the University of Bern, the University of Zurich, Charles University in Prague, ETH Zurich, and the University of Berlin. Later in life, he became a professor at the Institute for Advanced Study in Princeton. These roles highlight his significant contributions to theoretical physics across different academic settings.", "expert_answer": "Albert Einstein taught or held professorships at several institutions, including:\n\n- **University of Bern** — lecturer/Privatdozent  \n- **University of Zurich** — professor of theoretical physics  \n- **Charles University in Prague** — professor  \n- **ETH Zurich** — professor  \n- **University of Berlin** — professor, associated with the Prussian Academy of Sciences  \n- **Institute for Advanced Study in Princeton** — professor after emigrating to the U.S.\n\nHe also spent time as a visiting scholar/lecturer at places such as **Caltech**, but the main teaching appointments are the ones above.", "expert_latency_s": 6.78, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1768}
