{"id": "swebq0114", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.65, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2631, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Attila;Beowulf & Grendel;300;Dear Frankie;Butterfly on a Wheel;Gamer;Fast Food;Dracula 2000;Coriolanus", "query": "what movies gerard butler has been in?", "transcript": "What movies Gerard Butler has been in?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Gerard Butler has appeared in many films, including 300, The Phantom of the Opera, P.S. I Love You, Nim's Island, RocknRolla, The Ugly Truth, Gamer, Law Abiding Citizen, The Bounty Hunter, Machine Gun Preacher, Coriolanus, Olympus Has Fallen, London Has Fallen, Angel Has Fallen, Gods of Egypt, Geostorm, Den of Thieves, Hunter Killer, Greenland, Copshop, Last Seen Alive, Plane, and Kandahar. He also voiced Stoick in the How to Train Your Dragon films.", "expert_answer": "Gerard Butler has appeared in many films, including:\n\n- **300** (2006) — King Leonidas  \n- **The Phantom of the Opera** (2004) — The Phantom  \n- **P.S. I Love You** (2007)  \n- **Nim’s Island** (2008)  \n- **RocknRolla** (2008)  \n- **The Ugly Truth** (2009)  \n- **Gamer** (2009)  \n- **Law Abiding Citizen** (2009)  \n- **The Bounty Hunter** (2010)  \n- **Machine Gun Preacher** (2011)  \n- **Coriolanus** (2011)  \n- **Olympus Has Fallen** (2013)  \n- **London Has Fallen** (2016)  \n- **Angel Has Fallen** (2019)  \n- **Gods of Egypt** (2016)  \n- **Geostorm** (2017)  \n- **Den of Thieves** (2018)  \n- **Hunter Killer** (2018)  \n- **Greenland** (2020)  \n- **Copshop** (2021)  \n- **Last Seen Alive** (2022)  \n- **Plane** (2023)  \n- **Kandahar** (2023)  \n\nHe also voiced Stoick in the **How to Train Your Dragon** films.", "expert_latency_s": 5.32, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 2853}
{"id": "swebq0117", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.09, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.448, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Mendelian inheritance", "query": "what was gregor mendel contribution?", "transcript": "Gregor Mendel's contribution?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Gregor Mendel is known as the \"father of genetics.\" His contribution was discovering the basic laws of heredity through pea plant experiments, including the law of segregation, independent assortment, and dominance. He showed that traits are passed from parents to offspring through discrete units, now called genes.", "expert_answer": "Gregor Mendel is known as the **father of genetics**. His contribution was discovering the basic laws of heredity through pea plant experiments, including:\n\n- **Law of Segregation**\n- **Law of Independent Assortment**\n- **Law of Dominance**\n\nHe showed that traits are passed from parents to offspring through discrete units, now called **genes**.", "expert_latency_s": 1.91, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1371}
{"id": "swebq0120", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 3.53, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3633, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Government of Virginia", "query": "what was the government like in virginia colony?", "transcript": "What was the government like in Virginia colony?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Virginia had a representative colonial government. It was led by a royal governor appointed by the English king after Virginia became a royal colony in 1624. It also had an elected assembly called the House of Burgesses, founded in 1619, which was the first representative legislature in the English colonies. Only certain colonists, mainly free white male property owners, could vote or hold office. Local government was often run by county courts and wealthy landowning elites. So, it combined royal control from England with some self-government through elected representatives.", "expert_answer": "Virginia had a **representative colonial government**.\n\n- It was led by a **royal governor** appointed by the English king after Virginia became a royal colony in 1624.\n- It had an elected assembly called the **House of Burgesses**, founded in 1619, which was the first representative legislature in the English colonies.\n- Only certain colonists, mainly free white male property owners, could vote or hold office.\n- Local government was often run by county courts and wealthy landowning elites.\n\nSo, Virginia’s government combined **royal control from England** with **some self-government through elected representatives**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.05, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 2657}
{"id": "swebq0123", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.92, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2088, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Mathematician;Astronomer;Astrologer;Geographer;Philosopher", "query": "who was ptolemy and what did he do?", "transcript": "Who was Ptolemy, and what did he do?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Ptolemy was a Greek-Egyptian scientist who lived around 100 to 170 CE. He's famous for his work in astronomy, especially the geocentric model of the universe described in his book the Almagest. This idea that Earth was at the center of the cosmos dominated science for centuries. He also wrote important works on geography, astrology, and mathematics, making him one of the most influential scholars of the ancient world.", "expert_answer": "Ptolemy, also known as **Claudius Ptolemaeus** (c. 100–170 CE), was a **Greek-Egyptian astronomer, mathematician, geographer, and astrologer** who lived in Alexandria under the Roman Empire.\n\nHe is best known for:\n\n- **Astronomy:** He wrote the *Almagest*, which presented the **geocentric model** of the universe, placing Earth at the center with the Sun, Moon, planets, and stars moving around it. This model dominated astronomy for over 1,000 years.\n- **Geography:** He wrote *Geographia*, which compiled maps and coordinates of the known world and influenced mapmaking for centuries.\n- **Astrology:** He wrote the *Tetrabiblos*, an important ancient work on astrology.\n- **Mathematics and optics:** He contributed to trigonometry and studied light, vision, and refraction.\n\nIn short, Ptolemy was one of the most influential scientific thinkers of the ancient world, especially for his Earth-centered model of the cosmos.", "expert_latency_s": 4.1, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 2222}
