{"id": "swebq0168", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.86, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1287, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Zakāt;Salah;Hajj;Islamic dietary laws;Jihad;Sawm;Halal food;Shahada;Adab", "query": "what did the islamic people believe in?", "transcript": "What did the Islamic people believe in?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Islamic people, or Muslims, believe in one God, Allah, and follow the teachings of the Prophet Muhammad as recorded in the Qur'an. Their core beliefs are based on the Five Pillars of Islam, which include declaring faith in Allah, praying five times a day, giving to charity, fasting during Ramadan, and making a pilgrimage to Mecca if possible.", "expert_answer": "Islamic people (Muslims) believe in **one God, Allah**, and follow the teachings of **the Prophet Muhammad** as recorded in the **Qur’an**.\n\nCore beliefs include the **Five Pillars of Islam**:\n1. **Shahada** – declaration of faith in Allah and Muhammad as His messenger  \n2. **Salat** – prayer five times a day  \n3. **Zakat** – giving to charity  \n4. **Sawm** – fasting during Ramadan  \n5. **Hajj** – pilgrimage to Mecca if able", "expert_latency_s": 2.49, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1579}
