{"id": "swebq0237", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.81, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1639, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": "East Slavs;Europeans", "query": "where did russians originate?", "transcript": "Where did Russians originate?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Russians originated primarily among the **East Slavic peoples** of Eastern Europe. Their early cultural and political roots are usually traced to **Kievan Rus’** around the 9th to 13th centuries, a medieval state centered on cities like Kyiv, Novgorod, and later Vladimir-Suzdal. Over time, these Slavic-speaking communities mixed with neighboring Finnic, Baltic, Turkic, and other groups as they spread across western and central Russia.", "expert_answer": "Russians originated primarily among the **East Slavic peoples** of Eastern Europe. Their early cultural and political roots are usually traced to **Kievan Rus’** (9th–13th centuries), a medieval state centered around cities such as **Kyiv, Novgorod, and later Vladimir-Suzdal**.\n\nEthnically and culturally, Russians developed from East Slavic populations mixed over time with neighboring **Finnic, Baltic, Turkic, and other peoples**, especially as Slavic-speaking communities expanded across what is now western and central Russia.", "expert_latency_s": 3.1, "stall_ms": 25, "relay_ms": 2217}
{"id": "swebq0240", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.14, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2142, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Đắk Nông Province", "query": "where to go in vietnam beaches?", "transcript": "Where to go in Vietnam beaches?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Vietnam has some amazing beaches! If you're looking for top spots, Phu Quoc is often a favorite with its stunning islands and clear waters. Da Nang's My Khe Beach is also great, especially if you want a mix of city convenience and beach relaxation. Nha Trang offers lively nightlife and plenty of water activities, while Hoi An nearby provides a nice cultural touch. Mui Ne is perfect for kitesurfing and quiet dunes, and the Con Dao Islands are ideal if you prefer something more secluded and natural. Quy Nhon is another peaceful option with beautiful scenery. So, depending on what you're after—whether it's relaxation, adventure, or a bit of culture—you'll find plenty of great choices!", "expert_answer": "Top beach destinations in Vietnam:\n\n1. **Phu Quoc** – Best for island resorts, clear water, snorkeling, and relaxing beaches.  \n2. **Da Nang / My Khe Beach** – Easy to access, good city-beach mix, near Hoi An.  \n3. **Nha Trang** – Best for nightlife, island tours, diving, and beach resorts.  \n4. **Hoi An / An Bang Beach** – Great if you want culture plus a calm beach nearby.  \n5. **Mui Ne** – Famous for kitesurfing, sand dunes, and a relaxed vibe.  \n6. **Con Dao Islands** – Quiet, beautiful, less crowded, good for nature and diving.  \n7. **Quy Nhon** – Less touristy, scenic beaches, good seafood, peaceful atmosphere.\n\n**Best overall choice:** Phu Quoc for a classic beach holiday.  \n**Best beach + culture:** Da Nang/Hoi An.", "expert_latency_s": 6.06, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 3777}
{"id": "swebq0243", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.32, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2749, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Central Time Zone", "query": "what time is it in texas houston right now?", "transcript": "What time is it in Texas Houston right now?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Houston, Texas is in the Central Time Zone. On August 13, it's currently observing Central Daylight Time, which is UTC-5.", "expert_answer": "I don’t have access to the live current clock time.\n\nHouston, Texas is in the **Central Time Zone**. On **August 13**, it is typically **Central Daylight Time (CDT), UTC−5**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.19, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 688}
{"id": "swebq0246", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.41, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.17, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": "Federal government of Mexico", "query": "what type government does mexico have?", "transcript": "What type government does Mexico have?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Mexico has a **federal presidential constitutional republic**.", "expert_answer": "Mexico has a **federal presidential constitutional republic**.\n\nThis means it has:\n- A **president** as head of state and head of government\n- A **federal system** with power shared between the national government and states\n- A **constitution** that defines the government’s structure and powers", "expert_latency_s": 1.62, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 271}
{"id": "swebq0249", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.247, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Albert Gallatin;Mordecai Manuel Noah", "query": "who founded new york university?", "transcript": "Who founded New York University?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "New York University was founded in 1831 by Albert Gallatin and a group of prominent New Yorkers.", "expert_answer": "New York University was founded in 1831 by **Albert Gallatin** and a group of prominent New Yorkers.", "expert_latency_s": 2.11, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 508}
